  "notes": "Spain's birds are mostly modelled as rare or unknown in the database, so the list is hand-picked from the default regular species: what a visitor meets on a mainland tour (Doñana and the Guadalquivir marshes, Extremadura's dehesa and steppe, the Pyrenees, Ebro delta, Gibraltar strait and the Mediterranean coast), plus the Iberian specialities (Spanish Imperial Eagle, Iberian Magpie, Iberian Grey Shrike, Black Wheatear, Rufous-tailed Scrub Robin, Spotless Starling, Spanish Sparrow, White-headed Duck, Great Bustard). The Canary Islands birds (blue chaffinches, laurel pigeons, Canary Islands Chiffchaff, Fuerteventura Stonechat, Berthelot's Pipit) and the Balearic Warbler are dropped; Balearic Warbler is the only endemic, which would make a one-bird chapter. Northern and pelagic birds are dropped too. Spain has no endemic birds on the mainland, so the trip has no endemics chapter. The main chapter is Lookalikes from home.",
